A||N||1||4UMLA1||Goodies for 2.8||||7||
Z||000000||4UMLA1||12-30-2001||11:53 AM||||I was wondering what I could do to my 2.8 liter to make it have a little more balls to it.  Is the rebuild kit from the Fiero Store worth it to have it put in?  How about the exhaust, what kind could I install to give the engine more "umph" <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/luv4rez/images/10%20fiero%20gt%20.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||avengador1||12-30-2001||12:16 PM||||Change your catalytic converter to a free flow performance one. That is good for some H.P. You could also get headers or port your exhaust manifolds out. You could get the undersize pulleys, this will help the engine rev quicker. Finally get a good quality spark plug wire set and coil. All these changes can be done without taking your engine apart. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
